# The build context is copied twice by Nixpacks, so anything here is copied
# twice. More importantly, a stale node_modules or dist from a developer's
# machine would be copied over the image's own, which is how a build that
# looks clean runs code nobody built.
node_modules
dist
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
coverage

# .nixpacks is deliberately NOT ignored. The builder generates its Dockerfile
# and its nix expression into that directory and then COPYs the expression in,
# so excluding it fails the build at the third layer with "not found" for a
# file the builder had just written itself.
